# Virtualization

Sortable list of 5000 items, rendered through [`virtua`](https://github.com/inokawa/virtua) — only the rows visible in the viewport (plus a small buffer) live in the DOM.

`<DndDraggable>` is rendered inside `<VList>`'s `children` snippet, so each item registers a slot the moment virtua mounts it. `<DndDroppable>` wraps `<VList>` so the strategy still owns the list as a single drop container.

## `VirtualSource` adapter

Pass a `VirtualSource` to `sortable({ virtual })` so the strategy knows the **full** list length even when only a window of slots is mounted:

```ts
import type { VirtualSource } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const virtualSource: VirtualSource = {
    itemCount: () => items.length
    // getOffset/getSize are optional — reserved for future features
    // (drop into not-yet-mounted gaps, virtual preview rendering)
};

<DndDroppable strategy={sortable({ layout: 'vertical', virtual: virtualSource })} />
```

Without `virtual`, the strategy treats `slots.size` (mounted DOM nodes) as the list length — which is wrong for a virtualized list and breaks tail-position math for cross-container drops into the bottom of a long list.

> The bundled example above uses `virtua` — that's the virtualizer this integration has been tested with.

